4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing signals: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute auxiliary signals from the CSV: (a) return rate for that month vs the 24-month average return rate for the same region×product_line; (b) whether the following month's sales dropped sharply (if data available); (c) whether the spike is isolated (1-month) or sustained (2+ months). Save these diagnostic metrics to offline_data/stuffing_signals.csv → code_agent
5. Write Markdown report with embedded tables: Write a comprehensive Markdown report to offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md. Requirements: (1) H1 title; (2) at least one data table showing the top-3 anomalies with region, product_line, month, sales, 24-month mean, multiple, return_rate; (3) every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）'; (4) a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is more likely real demand or channel stuffing, citing the diagnostic signals; (5) no external data — all from the local CSV only → code_agent
